.TH NFC-READ-NDEF 1 "2026-06-27" "libnci 1.0.0-alpha.1" "libnci manual"
.SH NAME
nfc-read-ndef \- read and decode the NDEF message from a Type 4 tag
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nfc-read-ndef
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nfc-read-ndef
waits for an NFC Forum Type 4 tag (NTAG 424 DNA, a DESFire with an NDEF
application, ...), reads its NDEF message and prints a hex dump plus a decoded
view of the first record. Text and URI records are rendered as readable
strings.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --chip " PATH"
GPIO chip device node; autodetected when omitted.
.TP
.BI --bus " PATH"
I2C bus device node (default: /dev/i2c-1).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NCI_LOG
Log verbosity 0\(en5; set to 4 for NCI frame tracing, 5 to add raw I2C bytes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on a clean exit, non-zero if the device could not be opened.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
nfc-read-ndef
NCI_LOG=4 nfc-read-ndef
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nfc-write-ndef (1),
.BR nfc-poll (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Part of the libnci NFC stack.
